#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:1
msgid "Searching Satellite Data"
msgstr "搜索卫星数据"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:3
msgid ""
"Federated search across multiple providers simultaneously. Results are "
"deduplicated, scored, and returned sorted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:6
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:8
msgid ""
"A search begins with a description of what you are looking for, not with a "
"particular provider. You give pygeofetch an area (a bounding box or a "
"GeoJSON geometry), a date range and any filters that matter, such as maximum"
" cloud cover, satellite, processing level or resolution, and you name the "
"providers to ask. The same description is translated into each provider's "
"own API, the queries run in parallel, and the answers are merged into one "
"list of `SatelliteData` records that all look the same, whatever their "
"origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:10
msgid ""
"In practice a search session has three moves. Start broad, with a short list"
" of providers and a generous cloud-cover limit, to see how many scenes exist"
" and which satellites they come from. Narrow the query once you know what is"
" available, tightening dates or cloud cover until the list is a size you can"
" reason about. Then save the result, either as a GeoJSON file from the "
"command line or as the list returned by `client.search()` in Python, and "
"pass it to the download or streaming step. Results are cached for the "
"lifetime set by `cache_ttl`, so repeating a query while you refine "
"downstream steps does not cost another round trip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:12
msgid ""
"Two behaviours are useful to know before you rely on search in a script. A "
"provider that times out or fails is logged and left out rather than stopping"
" the search, so an empty list can mean that every provider failed, and the "
"log tells you which. And results are de-duplicated by provider and scene "
"identifier, so the same physical scene offered by two providers appears "
"twice; choose the provider you prefer for the download. The sections below "
"describe each filter and output format, and [Downloading](download.md) and "
"[Streaming](streaming.md) explain what to do with the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:14
msgid "What \"federated search\" actually does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:16
msgid ""
"Searching across multiple providers isn't just \"call each one and "
"concatenate the results\" — three steps happen after the raw per-provider "
"results come back:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:20
msgid ""
"**Per-provider search runs in parallel** (`max_search_workers`, default 8) —"
" a slow or unresponsive provider doesn't block the others; see `--on-"
"provider-failure` below for what happens if one errors out entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/data-access/search.md:24
msgid ""
"**Deduplication** — removes exact duplicates, keyed on "
"`f\"{provider}:{scene_id}\"`."
msgstr ""

